os-dev-report
{
  "issue": 12427,
  "status": "blocked",
  "branch": "claude/issue-12427-favorites-sidebar-menu",
  "pr": "https://github.com/objectstack-ai/objectui/pull/12443",
  "session": "session_019YFzJp4o8Ck4NsT1toC4UP — the Claude-Session id this subagent was stamped with (the parent seat's)",
  "premise_still_valid": true,
  "summary": "Neither half is complete. What landed is the in-surface groundwork, at adb45f8 in draft PR #12443 (body starts 'Part of #12427'). That is SidebarItemMenu (packages/app-shell/src/layout/SidebarItemMenu.tsx, with 15 tests), the one per-entry ⋯ menu for every entry type: Add/Remove favorites; Open in new tab and Copy link under the router basename, with an off-console URL used verbatim; Design for object/dashboard/page entries, gated isAdmin && canAuthorMetadata and routed to /apps/APP/metadata/TYPE/NAME; hover-only trigger; right-click opens it. Six new console.nav keys in all ten packs, and a minor changeset. BLOCKED 1, file surface: the hover pin control and the top Favorites section are not in UnifiedSidebar.tsx. NavigationRenderer in packages/layout/src/NavigationRenderer.tsx (@object-ui/layout) draws both: the pin is the SidebarMenuAction with the Pin/PinOff icon and the console.nav.pinItem label, and the section is its favoritesSection. No prop lets a host replace the per-row control or add rows to that section. The claim says stop on breach, so that file is untouched and UnifiedSidebar.tsx is unchanged (wiring the menu, merging the non-nav favorites to the top and deleting the group after Recent all need the layout slot). BLOCKED 2: #12436 is not yet on origin/main. The grep for 'No favorite star here since objectui#12423' on origin/main ObjectView.tsx printed 0 at 431cece; the control on the PR head 4ba299c printed 1. ObjectView.tsx and RecordDetailView.tsx are untouched. Premise note: on main the top section is already titled Favorites (console.nav.favorites, 收藏, star icon). Only the hover control still says pin.",
  "tests": "At adb45f8. (1) pnpm exec vitest run packages/app-shell/src/layout/__tests__/SidebarItemMenu-12427.test.tsx printed 'Tests 15 passed (15)'. The tests cover: object entry shows four entries to an admin who may author metadata (Design last), three to a non-admin and three to an admin without manage_metadata; Design navigates to /apps/crm/metadata/object/crm_lead; the favorites entry reads 'Remove from favorites' and toggles once; Open in new tab calls window.open('/_console/apps/crm/crm_lead','_blank','noopener,noreferrer'); Copy link writes the origin plus /_console/apps/crm/crm_lead; an off-console URL is used verbatim; a url entry has no Design; an action entry shows only the favorites entry; right-click opens the menu with the default prevented; sidebarItemDesignPath for page/object/dashboard, and null for url/component/separator. (2) pnpm exec vitest run packages/i18n/ (with the menu test) printed 'Test Files 84 passed (84)' and 'Tests 1336 passed | 13 skipped (1349)'. A verbose rerun of all-locales-key-parity, en-zh-key-parity and the menu test printed '63 passed (63)'. (3) pnpm --filter @object-ui/i18n --filter @object-ui/app-shell run type-check: VERDICT command-exit 0. It ran after building app-shell's dependency closure ('Tasks: 28 successful, 28 total'), and tsc -p tsconfig.test.json --listFilesOnly lists both new files. (4) Two ablations through objectstack scripts/ablation-replace.mjs; the test imports the source, so no dist is involved. Dropping canAuthorMetadata from the Design gate (anchor 1 to 0, blob 045e33c to d2ff3d7) failed exactly one test, 'lists exactly three for an admin the server refuses metadata authoring'. Dropping the absolute-URL test from offConsole (blob 045e33c to a5e449c) failed exactly one test, 'an external entry opens and copies its URL verbatim'. Each run was restored to the HEAD blob 045e33c with git diff HEAD empty. The first run of the menu test found a real bug (an absolute url entry without target was joined under the basename), fixed before commit.",
  "gates": "Local subset. All were run before any pipe and all exited 0: check:i18n-keys, check:i18n-dead-keys, check:i18n-drift ('6 key(s) added, 0 removed'), check:vi-mock-specifiers, check:vi-mock-inherit, check:vi-mock-override-shape, check:new-line-citations, check:control-bytes, check:test-path-roots, node scripts/check-changeset-presence.mjs ('12 source file(s) of 2 released package(s) changed, and this change declares 1 changeset'), and node scripts/check-changeset-no-major.mjs. objectui has no dispatch-gates.mjs, so there is no --ran reconciliation. I derived this list by hand from package.json check:* and the files the diff touches: locales, a test with vi.mock, new source, a changeset. CI check-runs on adb45f8 (36), read once at report time without polling: success for Changeset Bump Policy, Changeset Declaration, Changeset Fixed Group Check and label; skipped for Test (coverage), Test (coverage shard), dependabot; in_progress for Type Check, Lint, Repo Gates, Line Citation Gate, Governed Surface Queue Guard, Test (shard 1-16 of 16), Test (dist pins), Build & E2E, Build Docs, Bundle Analysis, Changeset Claim Re-read, Changeset Overwrite Report, Spec Main Shape Gate and Live E2E. CI convergence is the seat's.",
  "mcp_calls": "0 — no MCP GitHub tool was called",
  "api_writes": "2 relay dispatches, each POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches. One was pr_create: the relay ran POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectui/pulls (draft) and then POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectui/issues/12443/assignees with os-bill; the read-back was 6826 of 6826 bytes, identical. The other is this os-dev-report comment, which the relay posts as POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectui/issues/12427/comments. Two git pushes went outside REST: the empty-branch probe and adb45f8. No label writes: the brief named none, and the objectui labeler owns path labels.",
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "The sidebar half needs packages/layout/src/NavigationRenderer.tsx, which is outside the claimed surface. How should the next round get it?",
      "options": [
        "A: extend the surface to NavigationRenderer.tsx plus one layout test. Add two generic additive props: a per-row slot the host fills, drawn in place of the pin action, and host rows appended inside the Favorites section, which then renders when either kind of row exists. Hosts passing neither keep today's behaviour. The existing tests that click 'Pin NAME' by name are updated deliberately: UnifiedSidebar.pinnedOrder-12059.test.tsx, navItemVisibleEvaluated.test.tsx and the layout pin tests. Size S-M; resume from this branch.",
        "B: UnifiedSidebar draws the whole Favorites section itself and NavigationRenderer's section is switched off. This still needs a layout prop and an export of PinnedNavigationList, or else it loses the objectui#12059 drag order, so it is a bigger surface and duplicates rows.",
        "C: re-scope so that this card only moves the non-nav group, and the ⋯ menu goes to a later card. This is not workable either: merging into the top section needs the layout's favorites slot anyway."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because it is the smallest generic change, keeps one renderer and the pinned drag order, and SidebarItemMenu on this branch already fits it as is."
    },
    {
      "question": "Should Design also appear on report and doc entries? The metadata-admin router serves metadata/report/NAME and metadata/doc/NAME with editors, but the addendum names only page, object and dashboard.",
      "options": [
        "A: keep the three the addendum names (the branch does this)",
        "B: add report, and maybe doc"
      ],
      "recommendation": "A. It stays inside the addendum's enumeration, and adding a type later is one line in sidebarItemDesignPath plus one test."
    },
    {
      "question": "Two dashboard designers exist: metadata/dashboard/NAME, the metadata-admin router, and design/dashboard/NAME, DashboardDesignPage, which no in-tree link points at. Which one should Design open?",
      "options": [
        "A: metadata/dashboard/NAME (the branch does this)",
        "B: design/dashboard/NAME"
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because the brief says to use the metadata-admin router and it is the route PageView already uses for pages."
    },
    {
      "question": "The merged section's title and the labels of non-nav rows are not decided.",
      "options": [
        "A: title the merged section with console.nav.favorites (already Favorites / 收藏 with a star). A record or object favorite row shows its stored label (refreshLabel self-heals it) with a type icon, as the bottom group does today, and carries the same ⋯ menu, where the toggle removes it. Design shows for object, dashboard and page favorites (derived from the id), never for record or report. sidebar.favorites becomes unread and is deleted from ten packs; sidebar.removeFromFavorites stays for the console-home Starred group.",
        "B: resolve non-nav labels live, as useRecentItemLabel does"
      ],
      "recommendation": "A. There is no store change and no migration, and the labels match what Home shows."
    },
    {
      "question": "On mobile, enablePinning is off today, so there is no hover control. Should the ⋯ menu also be absent on mobile?",
      "options": [
        "A: absent on mobile, the same as today",
        "B: always visible on mobile"
      ],
      "recommendation": "A. It keeps the objectui#1055 hover-only rule and today's mobile behaviour."
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope_findings": []
}

