{
  "issue": 12427,
  "status": "blocked",
  "branch": "claude/issue-12427-favorites-sidebar-menu",
  "pr": "https://github.com/objectstack-ai/objectui/pull/12443",
  "session": "session_019YFzJp4o8Ck4NsT1toC4UP — the Claude-Session id this subagent was stamped with (the parent seat's)",
  "premise_still_valid": true,
  "summary": "Resumed from adb45f8 under scope note 6186841419. The head is 0bc0189, draft PR #12443, still 'Part of #12427'. LANDED, sidebar half: NavigationRenderer gets two additive props. renderItemAction is a host control drawn on every leaf and action row in place of the pin action. extraFavorites are host rows appended inside the Favorites section, which renders when either kind exists. A host passing neither keeps today's behaviour, drag order included. UnifiedSidebar fills the slot with SidebarItemMenu: one hover-revealed ⋯, right-click opens it, the favorites entry toggles through useNavPins().togglePin, Design shows for object/dashboard/page via metadata/TYPE/NAME, and there is no trigger on a phone. The non-nav favorites become rows of the top section with the same menu (the toggle removes them; Design comes from object:/dashboard:/page: ids). The group after Recent is gone, sidebar.favorites leaves the ten packs, and the store is untouched. LANDED, header half: #12436 reached origin/main (the grep printed 1 at a2225f9) and was merged in with a merge commit. The list header's actions row now ends with an icon-only ⋯ (named by the existing detail.moreActions key) holding the shared FavoriteMenuItem. useObjectListFavorite pins the app's own object nav entry when the member's shown navigation has one: one nav:ID with pinned true and no object: favorite. Otherwise it keeps object:NAME. The record page's overflow leads with sys_favorite (record:), ahead of Share. BLOCKED on ONE item: the record header still draws its star. RecordTitleChip draws it from the page:header renderer in packages/components/src/renderers/layout/containers.tsx, which is outside the surface. showStar defaults to true from the schema alone. If RecordDetailView stopped passing isFavorite/onToggleFavorite, the star would stay and store nothing (probe: one 'Add to favorites' button, aria-pressed false). So the wired star is kept, and the PR stays 'Part of'. CI on 0bc0189: 34 success, 3 skipped.",
  "tests": "At 0bc0189. NEW: SidebarItemMenu-12427 (15); NavigationRenderer.hostItemAction-12427 (8): slot in place of the pin, context href/external/label, no slot on group/separator, drawn with pinning off, host rows after pinned rows, null/false/[] count as none, default kept; UnifiedSidebar.favoritesMenu-12427 (10): one ⋯ and no pin per row, 4 entries for an admin and 3 for a non-admin, right-click, Add writes one nav:nav_leads pinned and then reads Remove, no trigger at 375px, stored object:/record: favorites in the top section with localStorage byte-identical, group labels exactly ['Favorites','Recent'], one section for pin plus stored favorite, Design on an object favorite and not on a record, Remove removes; ObjectView.favoritesEntry-12427 (3): no star button and the last control is an icon-only 'More actions', one nav:nav_projects (type nav, pinned true) and no object:, then 'Remove from favorites', then [] after the second press, object:showcase_project with label Projects and href /apps/demo/showcase_project when unlisted; RecordDetailView.favoritesEntry-12427 (2): overflow [Add to favorites, Share, ...], writes record:crm_call:rec-call-1 and then reads Remove. UPDATED deliberately: UnifiedSidebar.pinnedOrder-12059 drives the ⋯ menu ('More actions for NAME', then Add/Remove) instead of 'Pin NAME'; the starred record now reads '📋Acme' after the pinned rows. navItemVisibleEvaluated and the layout pin tests drive NavigationRenderer without the slot and pass unchanged. ABLATIONS (ablation-replace, each landed and was restored to the HEAD blob, git diff HEAD empty): leaf slot replaced by null, 8 red; hasExtraFavorites=false, 6 red; useObjectListFavorite's 'if (entry)' made false, 1 red ('writes one nav pin and no object favorite...'). UNION on 0bc0189: packages/layout/ + packages/app-shell/src/layout/ + packages/i18n/ + 24 other tests naming UnifiedSidebar/NavigationRenderer/SidebarItemMenu gave 'Test Files 218 passed (218)' and 'Tests 2512 passed | 13 skipped (2525)'. The RecordDetailView* and ObjectView* prefixes gave 'Test Files 124 passed (124)' and 'Tests 961 passed (961)'. TYPE-CHECK: pnpm --filter layout/i18n/app-shell run type-check, VERDICT command-exit 0, after rebuilding app-shell's closure (28/28; layout dist .d.ts carries renderItemAction). The test tsconfigs list the new tests (layout 1, app-shell 5). CI FIX: on head 122909d, Test (shard 5/16) failed objectView-config-keys-retired-4730.test.ts 'the namespace root survives, with the same surviving key shape in every pack': expected [ 'moreActions', …(102) ] to have a length of 102 but got 103. That was my new console.objectView.moreActions key. Fixed in 0bc0189 by dropping the key from all ten packs and naming the list ⋯ with the existing detail.moreActions (the record header's ⋯ name). No key was added and the ledger is untouched. That file alone: 5 passed; packages/i18n/: 85 files, 1331 passed and 13 skipped. CI shard 5/16 on 0bc0189 is success.",
  "gates": "Local, on the final diff, all run before any pipe and all exit 0: check:i18n-keys, check:i18n-dead-keys, check:i18n-drift, check:vi-mock-specifiers, check:vi-mock-inherit, check:vi-mock-override-shape, check:new-line-citations, check:control-bytes, check:test-path-roots, check-changeset-presence ('21 source file(s) of 3 released package(s) changed, and this change declares 1 changeset') and check-changeset-no-major. objectui has no dispatch-gates.mjs, so there is no --ran reconciliation; I derived the list by hand. CI check-runs on 0bc0189 (37), read once: 34 success (Type Check, Lint, Repo Gates, Line Citation Gate, Governed Surface Queue Guard, Test shards 1-16 of 16, Test, Test (dist pins), Build & E2E, Build Docs, Bundle Analysis, the five Changeset checks, Spec Main Shape Gate, Live E2E, label), 3 skipped.",
  "mcp_calls": "0 — no MCP GitHub tool was called",
  "api_writes": "This round: 1 relay dispatch, POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches, for the os-dev-report comment (POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectui/issues/12427/comments). No PR body PATCH; see the open question. 3 git pushes, outside REST: 6d2dfc2, 122909d, 0bc0189 (the last one includes 2b1006d), with merge commits 97a9d97 and 61dcd99, and no force-push. Earlier round: 2 dispatches (pr_create with assignees, and report comment 6186752694).",
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "Removing the record header star needs packages/components/src/renderers/layout/containers.tsx, which is outside the extended surface. How should the last acceptance item be closed?",
      "options": [
        "A: extend the surface to containers.tsx plus one components test. The page:header record chrome draws the star only when RecordContext carries onToggleFavorite (a star with no host toggle stores nothing). RecordDetailView drops isFavorite/onToggleFavorite, and the star's absence is pinned. The overflow entry is already in place. Size S; resume from 0bc0189.",
        "B: RecordDetailView sets showStar:false on the page:header nodes of the page it renders. This rewrites authored metadata at render time and fights an author's explicit showStar.",
        "C: keep the record star beside the overflow entry. This contradicts the card."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because it is one generic condition in the renderer, it removes the dead-star case for every host, and it leaves the authored showStar key meaning what it says."
    },
    {
      "question": "There is a conflict between the dispatch and os-dev.md on the PR body. The resume message and the scope note ask the dev to rewrite the PR body via relay issue_patch. os-dev.md says the dev writes the body once at pr_create and never PATCHes it; later changes are written by the seat. The body on #12443 still describes the stopped first round.",
      "options": [
        "A: the seat applies the replacement text I prepared at /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/b989e4d2-1086-5f1b-84ed-e7af367b27dd/scratchpad/issue-12427/12427-pr-body-v2.md (6429 bytes, first line 'Part of #12427', 'Clause-②: yes', no angle brackets, no closing keyword near another number)",
        "B: the dev patches it in a later round under an explicit exception"
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because os-dev.md says it wins where the two conflict. I did not PATCH."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which navigation entry does the list header pin when several match?",
      "options": [
        "A (implemented): the first object entry with this objectName and no recordId, in the member-shown tree, areas in order and then app.navigation. A pin on an entry in an area other than the sidebar's active one does not draw until that area is active, as for sidebar pins today.",
        "B: prefer the entry whose viewName matches the open view"
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because it is the plain reading of the card; B can come later if views get separate entries."
    },
    {
      "question": "Mobile: the non-nav favorite rows had an always-visible remove star below md. They now carry the ⋯ in the same place. Navigation rows get none, per decision 4. Keep that?",
      "options": [
        "A: keep it, so the phone keeps a way to remove a favorite from the sidebar",
        "B: no ⋯ on any row on a phone"
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because it preserves today's mobile control and decision 4 names only the rows that enablePinning governs."
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope_findings": [
    "carrier: objectui#12427 (its record-star item, open question 1) · RecordTitleChip, through the components page:header record chrome, draws a favorite star whenever schema showStar is not false. With no host onToggleFavorite it keeps the state locally and stores nothing. Measured once: the console record page passes the toggle, so the console itself is not dead today. Noted, not filed."
  ]
}
